  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="9dbe6d2d-a632-5aba-a27b-c942193d1843" activityNameId="92a88512-53b9-53f9-a472-84bd47e7221e" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Transport, average train, SBB mix</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Transport, average train, SBB mix
The operation, demand and maintanance of the train has been allocated based on the yearly train kilometric performance 0 Mio pkm. The demand of rail track has been allocated based on the demand of infrastructure per gross tonne kilometric performance in Switzerland 3.3E-8 km/gtkm. The losses at the overhead line are according to SBB 5.03%\nTechnology: For vehicle operation all technologies  are included in the average data. Rail construction addresses conventional gravel track beddings. For the manufacturing of vehicles, the data reflects the currently dominating train type (IC2000 and Kolibri) of Switzerland.\nTime period: Time of publications\nVersion: 1\nEnergy values: Undefined\n100.0\nProduction volume: Unknown\nLocal category: Transportsysteme\nLocal subcategory: Schiene\nUVEK 2022 source file:713_Transport-Train-passenger-CH_v0.7._X-Transport CH.xml\n\n
UUID: fc0800d8-7d2c-3d37-bcdc-34fc76b7b658
The module calls the modules  "production and maintenance of vehicles"; "construction and maintenance of railway tracks". The module includes the operation (energy consumption and emissione) of the train.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: For vehicle operation all technologies  are included in the average data. Rail construction addresses conventional gravel track beddings. For the manufacturing of vehicles, the data reflects the currently dominating train type (IC2000 and Kolibri) of Switzerland.
Time period: Time of publications
Production volume: na
Sampling: Statistics 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_fc0800d8-7d2c-3d37-bcdc-34fc76b7b658.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
